      "prompts": {
        "short": "Implement WI-001: adopt and verify the selected identity template; Story Ref: N/A (Identity infrastructure).\nEntry: {{APPLICATION_REPOSITORY}}, template https://github.com/ColmKenna/IdentityServerWithAdminTemplate.git at {{TEMPLATE_REVISION}}.\nCreate chore/wi-001-adopt-selected-identity-template from {{INTEGRATION_BRANCH}} before edits. Preserve upstream security and migration behavior.\nHuman drives the integration choices. Resolve each placeholder from the approved application decisions and predecessor code. If a required value is still missing, stop and ask; never invent a value. An unrelated later-phase decision does not block this item.\nSuppress automatic attribution: no Co-Authored-By trailers, generated-with footers, model names or AI badges in commits.\nStop at a green, committed, pushed branch and report its name, commits and test results. Do not merge, rebase onto the integration branch, fast-forward, force-push or delete branches; the developer decides integration.",
        "full": "WI-001 — Adopt and verify the selected identity template\n\nStory Ref: N/A (Identity infrastructure). This prerequisite comes from the user's explicit template choice and the generator stack; it implements no invented business story.\n\nUse .NET 10, Aspire, Razor Pages with a server-side BFF and EF Core for the online application (generator defaults, inferred). Reuse IdentityServerWithAdminTemplate for authentication, identity configuration and security administration. Preserve the verified template package, language and test conventions. Browser access/refresh tokens remain server-side at the BFF. Business API endpoints are owned by the Field Sales API, behind the BFF for website calls; tablet Sync calls are direct and authenticated.\n\nSOURCE: https://github.com/ColmKenna/IdentityServerWithAdminTemplate.git\nThe accessible README describes the foundation. Deeper source inspection was not executed because automatic approval review reached a usage limit; verify actual source at {{TEMPLATE_REVISION}} before adoption.\n\nDEPENDENCIES: none. Application checkout {{APPLICATION_REPOSITORY}}. Rename prefix {{TEMPLATE_PREFIX}}. Resolve each placeholder from the approved application decisions and predecessor code. If a required value is still missing, stop and ask; never invent a value. An unrelated later-phase decision does not block this item.\n\nHUMAN WORK PACKAGE:\n1. In {{APPLICATION_REPOSITORY}}, adopt https://github.com/ColmKenna/IdentityServerWithAdminTemplate.git at {{TEMPLATE_REVISION}}; inspect actual source and record the upstream commit before changes.\n2. Use the template rename script preview and review the proposed {{TEMPLATE_PREFIX}} changes before applying; preserve its migration history.\n3. Verify its identity host, security administration, Aspire resources and existing tests. Keep existing packages and conventions until compatibility has been demonstrated.\n4. Prepare the staff web/BFF and business API registration contracts consumed by WI-002; remove sample client assumptions and use application-owned configuration.\n5. Characterise role/admin access and logout behavior. Record which application-specific role revocation and tablet-session rules are still delivered by later cards.\n6. Agree the application git workflow and concrete solution paths before dependent items start.\n\nDECISIONS: Pin the upstream revision, application repository, prefix, integration branch and client boundaries. Decide business-role mapping with WI-002; do not equate Head Office User with SysAdmin.\nDELEGABLE SLIVERS: type the approved registration/options configuration; run and diagnose existing template tests; implement the human-agreed baseline checks.\n\nCONTRACT: The template identity host owns OIDC protocol endpoints and /Admin directly, outside the Field Sales BFF. AppHost owns orchestration. Staff web/BFF and business API contracts are established for WI-002; do not implement catalogue, tablet or customer invitation behavior here.\n\nTEST OWNERSHIP: Human-Led. Agree the matrix first; implement tests named Should_ExpectedBehaviour_When_Condition.\nShould_StartTheIdentityHost_When_ThePinnedTemplateIsConfigured — Verify the existing solution, migrations and baseline test suite before changing application behavior.\nShould_DenySecurityAdministration_When_TheUserLacksSysAdmin — Use the template's normal nonadministrator user to prove /Admin is protected before adding business roles.\nShould_KeepRevokedAdministrationRevoked_When_TheHostRestarts — Characterise the template's documented administrator behavior at the actual adopted revision.\n\nGIT: Create chore/wi-001-adopt-selected-identity-template from current {{INTEGRATION_BRANCH}} before edits. Commit the clean adoption, reviewed renaming/configuration, then baseline verification as separate buildable parts. Format: chore(wi-001): <imperative summary>\nRefs: WI-001.\nSuppress automatic attribution: no Co-Authored-By trailers, generated-with footers, model names or AI badges in commits.\nRun the full existing template/application suite and build without new warnings before pushing; report failures and stop if not green. Stop at a green, committed, pushed branch and report its name, commits and test results. Do not merge, rebase onto the integration branch, fast-forward, force-push or delete branches; the developer decides integration."
      }
